.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
.Dd June 11, 2026
.Dt EMACS-JOURNAL-2026-06-11 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-journal-2026-06-11
.Nd working notes of 2026-06-11
.Sh ENTRIES
.Ss Upstream survey + realign emacs.nix (nixpkgs emacs31, cached overlay variants, Darwin patch cleanup)
.Ss Summary
Surveyed upstream nixpkgs, nix-community/emacs-overlay, and nix-giant/nix-darwin-emacs (source of our macOS patches) against our packaging.
Several upstream moves in the last week invalidated assumptions in
.Ql "emacs.nix" :
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fBnixpkgs ships
.Ql "emacs31"
again\fP (31.0.90 prerelease, added 2026-06-05, Hydra-cached, plus
.Ql "emacs31-gtk3/-nox/-pgtk" ).
Our 2026-06-05 journal rationale for basing mainline on the overlay's
.Ql "emacs-git"
(\(dqemacs31 attribute no longer exists in nixpkgs\(dq) went stale within the week.
.It
\fBemacs-overlay ships prebuilt
.Ql "emacs-unstable"
and
.Ql "emacs-igc" Ns No "\fP"
(and pgtk siblings), all cached on nix-community.cachix.org with daily-updated rev pins.
Our
.Ql "unstable" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "igc"
variants instead overrode
.Ql "emacs-git" Ns No "'s"
.Ql "src"
with
.Ql "lib.fakeHash" ,
forcing the
.Ql "--argstr hash"
dance and a from-source build every time.
.It
\fBnix-darwin-emacs dropped
.Ql "fix-window-role.patch"
from
.Ql "patches-31/" Ns No "\fP"
(fixed upstream in Emacs 31) and added
.Ql "adjust-ns-init-colors.patch"
to
.Ql "patches-unstable/" .
Our
.Ql "withFixWindowRolePatch"
was doubly dead: its
.Ql "patchBranch == \(dq30\(dq"
gate could never be true, and the file it pointed at no longer exists.
Separately, macport (Emacs 30.x) mapped to
.Ql "patches-31"
— the wrong branch.
.It
\fBnixpkgs
.Ql "emacs30-macport" Ns No "\fP"
now builds from the jdtsmith/emacs-mac fork (Mitsuharu's original is dormant) and does \fBnot\fP override
.Ql "srcRepo" ,
so the make-emacs default
.No \&( Ns Ql "true" )
applies — our
.Ql "srcRepo = false"
for macport silently busted its cache.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "withXwidgets"
default divergence\fP: our extra
.Ql "isDarwin"
clause was a leftover mirror of the overlay's
.Ql "withXwidgets = false"
override; with mainline on nixpkgs
.Ql "emacs31"
it would have broken parity for
.Ql "withPgtk = true"
builds vs
.Ql "emacs31-pgtk" .
.El
.Ss Changes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "emacs.nix" Ns No "\fP"
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Base package map:
.Ql "mainline"
→ nixpkgs
.Ql "emacs31" ;
.Ql "git" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "unstable" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "igc"
→ the overlay's
.Ql "emacs-git" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "emacs-unstable" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "emacs-igc" ;
.Ql "macport"
→ nixpkgs
.Ql "emacs-macport"
alias (emacs-overlay ships no macport).
.It
Source overrides only apply with an explicit
.Ql "--argstr rev" ;
default revisions ride the overlay/nixpkgs pins.
Dropped the manual
.Ql "gitMeta" Ns No "/fakeHash"
plumbing, the duplicate aarch64
.Ql "--enable-check-lisp-object-type" ,
and the manual igc
.Ql "--with-mps=yes"
+
.Ql "mps"
buildInput
.No \&( Ns Ql "pkgs.emacs-igc"
already carries them, and
.Ql "makeOverridable"
replays its
.Ql "overrideAttrs"
layers through
.Ql ".override" ).
.It
.Ql "srcRepo ? true"
for all variants (matches upstream; every base is a git checkout now that nixpkgs fetches via fetchgit/fetchFromGitHub).
.It
.Ql "withXwidgets"
default now matches upstream make-emacs.nix:
.Ql "!noGui && (withGTK3 || withPgtk || withNS || variant == \(dqmacport\(dq)" .
.It
Darwin patches: removed
.Ql "withFixWindowRolePatch" ;
added
.Ql "withAdjustNsInitColorsPatch"
(patches-unstable only, i.e. git/igc);
.Ql "patchBranch"
now maps macport →
.Ql "\(dq30\(dq" ;
replaced every
.Ql "lib.fakeHash"
with pinned per-branch fetchpatch hashes (31 and unstable currently carry byte-identical patch content; 30 differs).
.El
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "CLAUDE.md" Ns No "\fP"
— cache-parity section retargeted to
.Ql "pkgs.emacs31"
(+ per-variant overlay parity checks in the verify snippet); base-package map and the \(dqfails on first run, reports hash\(dq wording corrected.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "Justfile" Ns No "\fP"
—
.Ql "build-git"
comment no longer claims a hash dance.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "flake.nix" Ns No "\fP"
— emacs-overlay input comment: the overlay now only supplies the git-based variants; mainline comes from nixpkgs.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "docs/" Ns No "\fP"
.No \&( Ns Ql "introduction.mdx" ,
.Ql "installation.mdx" ,
.Ql "architecture/overview.mdx" ,
.Ql "architecture/nix-build.mdx" )
— parity target, variant table, IGC/Git-variant sections, and hash-dance notes updated to match the new base-package map.
.El
.Ss Verification
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Parity eval is
.Ql "true"
for \fBall four\fP default-rev variants:
.Ql "mainline == pkgs.emacs31" ,
.Ql "git == pkgs.emacs-git" ,
.Ql "unstable == pkgs.emacs-unstable" ,
.Ql "igc == pkgs.emacs-igc" .
.It
.Ql "nix-build emacs.nix --dry-run"
→ \(dqwill be fetched (75.1 MiB)\(dq, i.e. a pure Hydra substitution; no compilation.
.It
Darwin patch / macport / custom-rev paths instantiate cleanly
.No \&( Ns Ql "nix-instantiate"
with
.Ql "system = \(dqaarch64-darwin\(dq"
and a dummy rev).
.It
.Ql "nixfmt"
clean;
.Ql "nix flake check"
green.
.El
.Ss Watch items (no action yet)
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "__structuredAttrs"
enabled\fP for Emacs on nixpkgs master 2026-06-08 — not in our pin
.No \&( Ns Ql "8c3cede7" );
lands at the next
.Ql "just update" .
Our
.Ql "overrideAttrs"
list/string manipulation is compatible, but re-run the parity eval after the bump.
.Ql "strictDeps = true"
is already at our pin.
.It
\fBhomebrew-emacs-plus\fP has a
.Ql "fix-ns-x-colors.patch"
for Emacs 31 that nix-darwin-emacs has \fInot\fP adopted; their
.Ql "adjust-ns-init-colors.patch"
(unstable branch only) is the alternative approach to the same headless-dump color problem.
.It
nix-darwin-emacs has no
.Ql "patches-32/"
directory yet, while homebrew-emacs-plus added emacs-32 targets in May 2026 — if Emacs 32 patch branches appear,
.Ql "patchBranch"
may need a new mapping.
.It
The mainline base is now the 31.0.90 \fBprerelease\fP; nixpkgs will bump it through the 31.x release cycle, with each bump arriving via
.Ql "just update"
as a cache hit.
.El
